==Reconstruction==
{{main|Proto-Munda language}}
The proto-forms have been reconstructed by Sidwell & Rau (2015: 319, 340–363).<ref name="SidwellRau2015">Sidwell, Paul and Felix Rau (2015). "Austroasiatic Comparative-Historical Reconstruction: An Overview." In Jenny, Mathias and Paul Sidwell, eds (2015). ''The Handbook of Austroasiatic Languages''. Leiden: Brill.</ref> Proto-Munda reconstruction has since been revised and improved by Rau (2019).<ref>Rau, Felix. (2019). ''Advances in Munda historical phonology''. Zenodo. {{doi|10.5281/zenodo.3380908}}</ref><ref>Rau, Felix. (2019). ''Munda cognate set with proto-Munda reconstructions'' (Version 0.1.0) [Data set]. Zenodo. {{doi|10.5281/zenodo.3380874}}</ref>

== Writing systems ==
The following are current used alphabets of Munda languages:

* [[Mundari Bani]] (Mundari alphabet)<ref>{{Cite web |date=19 January 2024 |title=Atlas of Endangered Alphabets: Indigenous and minority writing systems, and the people who are trying to save them. |url=https://www.endangeredalphabets.net/mundari-bani/ |access-date=4 February 2025 |language=en-US}}</ref>
* [[Ol Chiki script|Ol Chiki]] (Santali alphabet)<ref>{{Cite web |title=Santali language and alphabets |url=https://www.omniglot.com/writing/santali.htm |access-date=4 February 2025 |website=www.omniglot.com}}</ref>
* [[Ol Onal]] (Bhumij alphabet)<ref>{{Cite web |title=Ol Onal alphabet |url=https://www.omniglot.com/writing/olonal.htm |access-date=4 February 2025 |website=www.omniglot.com}}</ref>
* [[Sorang Sompeng script|Sorang Sompeng]] (Sora alphabet)<ref>{{Cite web |date=30 November 2018 |title=Atlas of Endangered Alphabets: Indigenous and minority writing systems, and the people who are trying to save them. |url=https://www.endangeredalphabets.net/alphabets/sorang-sompeng/ |access-date=4 February 2025 |language=en-US}}</ref>
* [[Warang Citi]] (Ho alphabet)<ref>{{Cite web |title=Warang Citi alphabet |url=https://www.omniglot.com/writing/varangkshiti.htm |access-date=4 February 2025 |website=www.omniglot.com}}</ref>

